    "durationMs": 270116,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener API is complete and fully tested. Here's what I built:\n\n**Implementation**\n- Created a Laravel 11.57 project in `/workspace` (scaffolded elsewhere, merged in around the existing `.git`), with `vendor/` installed via Composer.\n- `bootstrap/app.php` registers `routes/api.php` with `apiPrefix: ''`, so routes live at `/links` and `/r/{code}`, not `/api/...`.\n- `Link` model + Eloquent migration (`code` unique varchar(20), `url` text, `clicks` unsigned bigint) — persistence is plain MySQL via the `DB_*` env vars, which I verified are the only DB source (`DB_CONNECTION=sqlite` was removed from `.env`).\n- `LinkController` (store/show/index) and `RedirectController` (`302` + `Location`, atomic `increment('clicks')`), with a `ValidHttpUrl` rule enforcing absolute http/https URLs with a host, and a `^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}$` regex for codes; auto-generated codes are 8 alphanumeric chars with collision retries, and a unique-constraint catch returns 409 as a race safety net.\n- `start.sh` runs `php artisan migrate --force` then `exec php artisan serve --host=0.0.0.0 --port=8000 --no-reload` in the foreground — I confirmed in the framework source that without `--no-reload`, `serve` strips all non-passthrough env vars when a `.env` exists, so this flag is what keeps requests on the same MySQL database as migrations.\n- README rewritten with startup instructions and endpoint docs.\n\n**Verified by live HTTP tests** (then restarted the server to prove persistence): 201 with unchanged URL and `clicks: 0`, 409 on duplicate custom code, 404 JSON for unknown codes, 422 JSON with `error` for malformed JSON, missing/invalid URLs (no scheme, `ftp://`, `http://`, scheme-relative) and bad codes (too short/long, bad chars, non-string), 302 with exact `Location`, exactly-once click increments, ascending `{\"items\": [...], \"total\": N}` list order, and data surviving a full restart. Port 8000 is now free for the grader to run `sh start.sh`."
  }
